would `SIGSEGV` here rather than silently pass.\n- **NULL** asserted to produce the *same fatal signal*, run in a child process — both die with SIGSEGV (exit 139), verified non-trivially rather than \"both failed somehow\".\n- **Out-of-range enum values**: there is no `enum` parameter, so the real analogue is the raw bit-fields; both no-valid-variant encodings (layer `00`, rate `15`) are covered.\n- **`-O2` cross-check**: since rows 1–3 depend on link layout, I rebuilt the C with `-O2` in a scratch dir and re-ran the full 65536 sweep — still byte-identical, so the zero-padding model isn't an artifact of one build.\n\n## Two things worth flagging\n\n1. **`cargo test` alone does not build the cdylib.** With `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]` and no `rlib`, cargo builds the test binaries but never the `.so`, so the tests initially failed to find it. The harness now builds it on demand — a plain `cargo test` works.\n2. **crates.io is unreachable** from this sandbox, but `libloading` and `libc` were in the local cargo cache, so I added `.cargo/config.toml` with `offline = true`. If you build elsewhere you may want to drop that.\n\nFiles added under `translation/`: `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `tests/{common/mod.rs,valid_path.rs,error_path.rs,symbol_parity.rs}`, `verify_all.sh`. `c_src/` is unmodified (md5s of all three sources unchanged; only `build/` added)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":485,"cache_read_input_tokens":102934,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":485,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e1fb8005-5578-46ec-ac9e-6f45e5da1c1b","uuid":"23d4bbd5-edb5-4d45-b971-b8b4dbfc5172","timestamp":"2026-08-26T22:03:42.757Z"}
